<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  MediVault supervisor LaunchAgent (SMAppService.agent contract).

  This plist ships INSIDE the app bundle at
  MediVault.app/Contents/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.medivault.supervisor.plist
  and is registered from the desktop app via SMAppService.agent.register()
  (ServiceManagement.framework, macOS 13+). It is the USER-scoped agent:
  the backend runs while the doctor is logged in, independent of the
  desktop window. NO root, NO LaunchDaemon.

  PATH MODEL (production hardening):
    BundleProgram  is the app-bundle RELATIVE path to the supervisor
                   (launchd.plist(5): "an app-bundle relative path to the
                   executable for the job. This key is only supported for
                   plists that are installed using SMAppService"). The
                   previous absolute /Applications/… Program key is GONE —
                   it broke per-user installs (~/Applications) and embedded
                   a machine-location assumption.
    No arguments:  the supervisor defaults to the `run` subcommand and
                   resolves its config exe-relatively at
                   ../Resources/supervisor-config.json, whose bundle paths
                   are themselves Contents/-relative. The whole chain is
                   install-location independent.

  Other fields (acceptance/macos-architecture-audit.md, SMAPPSERVICE DESIGN):
    RunAtLoad      true  — starts at login
    KeepAlive      true  — launchd restarts the supervisor itself on crash
    ProcessType    Background — App Nap / scheduling class for a daemon-like agent
    ExitTimeOut    90    — seconds before launchd SIGKILLs on shutdown;
                           the supervisor's own graceful window is bounded
                           inside this budget
    Disabled       false

  NOTES
    - No StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath: launchd capture paths must be
      per-user ABSOLUTE, which cannot be known at bundle-build time. The
      supervisor performs its own structured file logging into
      ~/Library/Logs/MediVault/ (supervisor.log, postgres.log, api.log);
      pre-logging early crashes are observable via the unified log:
        log show (predicate: process == "mediavault-supervisor")
    - The supervisor's own crash resilience is redundant by design with
      KeepAlive (launchd = outer ring, supervisor restart backoff = inner
      ring for the CHILDREN).
    - Registration/UX (Login Items approval pane) is an interactive-Mac
      proof, NOT a CI proof; CI proves the helper's status model, the
      plist contract, and the foreground lifecycle of the same binary.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>dev.medivault.supervisor</string>

    <key>BundleProgram</key>
    <string>Contents/MacOS/mediavault-supervisor</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <key>Disabled</key>
    <false/>

    <key>ExitTimeOut</key>
    <integer>90</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
